  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Chemical Technician, Advanced Certificate - Pathway 1 (Fall Start)' program map, Catalog 2025-26, published July 21, 2025 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/6976/PublishedPdf). Start Term: Fall. This is a Certificate of Achievement (a grade of C or better is required in each major course). Official Total Units: 17-18 = 5+5+6+1 = 17 at the low end, verified against the map's 5-6 / 5 / 6 / 1 headers. The map is split First Year (Semesters 1-2) and Second Year (Semesters 3-4) as printed. The modeled path uses the first-listed options at the low end of variable units: ENGL C1000 (3) for the Semester 1 *Major Elective slot (a minimum of 3 units from: ENGL C1000, ENGWR 488(H), ENGL C1001, ENGL C1001H, ESLW 340). In-plan prereqs sequenced (all with grades of C or better): CHEMT 424 requires CHEM 410 or CHEM 420 - the modeled in-plan selection is CHEM 410 (both listed in the map; CHEM 410 is the in-plan choice, documented here); CHEMT 429 requires CHEM 410; BUS 310 requires BUS 100, ENGL C1000, or ESLW 340 - the modeled in-plan selection is ENGL C1000 (the alternative options are documented here); CHEMT 297 requires CHEMT 201, 424 and 429. The counselor note documents that this program has many chemistry prerequisites (CHEM 401 prerequisite for CHEM 410 is external to this plan; students are encouraged to contact a counselor for course sequence adjustments). Pathway 1 is recommended for students who want to pursue analytical techniques (emphasis on quantitative analysis); Pathway 2 is recommended for students who plan to pursue organic analysis. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
